The extinction probability $q = PP(X_n = 0 "for some" n >= 0)$ of a branching process with offspring probability generating function $G(z) = EE[z^(X_1)]$ satisfies
$
  q_(n+1) = G(q_n), quad q = G(q),
$
and is the minimal non-negative solution of $G(x) = x$; moreover $q < 1$ if and only if $EE[X_1] > 1$.
